=== Ciphertext-only length threshold — crib-free climb on known M4 keys ===
corpus        : Fixtures/u534_corpus.json
controls      : 48 published 1 May 1945 U-534 keys (lengths 60…719), using 8
trigram model : Fixtures/german_trigrams.txt (14947 grams; letters=28508834 ic=0.0747 distinct=14947)
scorers       : staged
exhaustion    : Ostwald partial exhaustion over the 6 most frequent ciphertext letters
                (applied symmetrically to true *and* wrong settings)
wrong samples : 6 random message keys per cell, same shell (the hardest negative control — a real sweep also enumerates wrong wheel
                orders and rings, which are easier to reject, so margins here
                are conservative)
target        : P1030680 is 72 letters. Published record for this attack class
                is 78 letters on three-rotor Heer; this is four-rotor naval M4.

preflight     : 32/48 controls decrypt to their published plaintext under their published key
  FAILED to round-trip (key mapping is wrong for these):
